# ~/.wslconfig.local — your machine-specific WSL2 tuning (memory, processors).
# install.ps1 creates this file once and never touches it again, unlike
# ~/.wslconfig itself which gets re-rendered from wsl/.wslconfig.template on
# every install.ps1 run. If ~/.wslconfig already existed before dotfiles
# managed it, install.ps1 carries its [wsl2] settings forward into this file
# automatically the first time it runs, instead of discarding them.
#
# Changes to ~/.wslconfig only take effect after `wsl --shutdown` (this stops
# every running WSL distro, so install.ps1 never runs it for you).

# ── example ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# [wsl2]
# memory=8GB
# processors=8
